Core patch api-deployment-role-name (CP-1210)

VAMS fork core patch for GitHub issue #1210: the REST API's AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment gets its
logical id from a hash of the OpenAPI spec only (rest-api-gateway-construct.ts,
deployment.addToLogicalId(spec)). The spec names the authorizer invoke role through an unresolved
Fn::GetAtt, whose hashed form does not change when only the role's name changes. Switching the
role-name prefix (cdk.json environments.aws.IamRoleNamePrefix, read by the IamRoleTransform aspect;
vra's iam.mode boundary sets it) replaces every role, but no new Deployment is created, so the
stage keeps serving a snapshot whose authorizer credentials name the deleted role: every route,
authenticated or anonymous, answers HTTP 500 AuthorizerConfigurationException.

This patch also hashes the literal prefix into the Deployment's logical id when it is set. An empty
prefix adds nothing, so a deployment without a prefix keeps its logical id (no redeploy). A changed
prefix creates a new Deployment that names the new role. It does not change any role or the spec.

Made against VAMS v2.6.6 (line 327) and also applies to development a9ac094c4 (line 354): the hunk
keeps one trailing context line because the line after it differs between the two. Activate: copy
this file to <home>/ledger/core-patches/ and list it in core-patches.md (see
ledger-template/core-patches.md). Needed together with CP-431 whenever iam.mode is boundary with a
rolePrefix, on an upgrade over a deployment that ran without that prefix. Retire the entry when
upstream fixes GitHub issue #1210 (the engine reports the patch as "present" once the fork has it).

diff --git a/infra/lib/nestedStacks/apiLambda/constructs/rest-api-gateway-construct.ts b/infra/lib/nestedStacks/apiLambda/constructs/rest-api-gateway-construct.ts
--- a/infra/lib/nestedStacks/apiLambda/constructs/rest-api-gateway-construct.ts
+++ b/infra/lib/nestedStacks/apiLambda/constructs/rest-api-gateway-construct.ts
@@ -324,4 +324,19 @@
         });
 
         const deployment = new apigw.Deployment(this, "Deployment", { api: this.restApi });
+        // Core patch api-deployment-role-name (GitHub issue #1210): the spec names the authorizer
+        // invoke role through an unresolved GetAtt, whose hash does not change when only the role's
+        // name changes. A new role-name prefix (cdk.json environments.aws.IamRoleNamePrefix, read by
+        // the IamRoleTransform aspect) replaces every role, so without this the stage keeps serving
+        // a deployment whose authorizer credentials name a deleted role (HTTP 500 on every route).
+        // Hashing the literal prefix in forces a new deployment; an empty prefix adds nothing, so
+        // the logical id of a deployment without a prefix stays as it was.
+        const iamRoleNamePrefix = this.node.tryGetContext("environments")?.aws?.IamRoleNamePrefix;
+        if (
+            typeof iamRoleNamePrefix === "string" &&
+            iamRoleNamePrefix !== "" &&
+            !cdk.Token.isUnresolved(iamRoleNamePrefix)
+        ) {
+            deployment.addToLogicalId({ iamRoleNamePrefix });
+        }
         deployment.addToLogicalId(spec); // any spec change -> new deployment -> auto redeploy
